# roles
tf-tide-teller-e5	The tide-teller of the Deepwater era: an older woman, the sea-reading sage dressed as a hermit, weathered kind face, sea-glass spectacles pushed up into windblown grey hair, a shawl of knotted kelp-cord over an oilskin, a rolled kelp chart under one arm, a small brass storm-glass on a cord at her throat, eyes bright with warm eccentricity.
tf-cannery-hand-e5	The cannery-hand of the Deepwater era: the newcomer kid of the Steamworks years now grown into a young adult with a weathered open face, a cannery apron over a rolled-sleeve work shirt, a small folded paper boat held in one hand like an old habit, salt-cracked knuckles, a quiet vindicated smile.
tf-harbormaster-e5	The harbormaster of the Deepwater era: a woman in a wheelhouse coat with brass buttons, a steady level gaze, a retired stub of manifest chalk hanging on a cord at her collar, hair tied back against the wind, the calm authority of someone the flood appointed and the town confirmed.
tf-shipwright-e5	The shipwright of the Deepwater era: a broad-shouldered figure in an oilskin apron dusted with sawdust, an adze resting on one shoulder, calloused hands, a face that learned its trade in grief and learned it well, warm and tired.
tf-pearl-diver-e5	The pearl-diver of the Deepwater era: a lean diver with wet hair pushed back, a knotted net bag and a small diving knife on a belt, salt-pale skin, a mother-of-pearl button at the throat, calm unhurried eyes used to holding breath.
tf-he3-assayer-e8	The He-3 assayer of the Orbital era: an assayer of the old assay lineage in a suit-brass collar with a glass visor pushed up, silver-and-teal orbital garb, a jeweller's loupe on a chain, a small sealed glass vial held up to the light, a precise kind face and silver hair.
tf-eldest-heir-e10	The eldest heir of the Deep Sky era: the old rival's line grown kind, a young man in an Ark-yard coat with a working pocket watch on a chain, a small crossed-pickaxes emblem stitched on the lapel, an open half-laughing face that has just been told yes.
tf-baron-e10	The Baron of the Deep Sky era, ancient now: the old rival turned caretaker of the canals on the red world, a lined weathered face gone gentle, a canal-keeper's staff in one hand, a worn coat with a faded crossed-pickaxes crest, eyes that once declared everything spent and now keep the greenest thing they ever touched.
tf-quack-e10	The Quack of the Deep Sky era, ancient and freed: the old medicine-show man, a threadbare showman's coat and a dented tonic bottle held like a relic, long white hair, a face that spent a century in a cell and now sits at the far end of a long table, warm, unnamed, never grim.
tf-charter-keeper-e10	The Charter-Keeper of the Deep Sky era: the custodian of the Charter Press hall, a middle-aged figure in a printer's apron with ink-stained hands, a small glass jar holding a single bright mote of light set on the desk before them, the brass handle of a child-height lever just in frame, a patient proud face.
